{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788304594,"nonce":"wTJsKhvb9h1KG5KVwivLhf9U9lQ=","title":"Observers flush the region updater: GetRoom can rebuild rooms and write scribed state","message":"Found while implementing 261f2e9 (temperature), by auditing every getter the two\nnew files reach. It is NOT a defect of that work — it is a property of the whole\nobservation surface that predates it, and the fix belongs to all of it at once.\n\n## What is true\n\nEvery observer that asks \"what room is this in\" goes through\n`Verse/RegionAndRoomQuery.GetRoom` (the `IntVec3` and the `Thing` overload\nalike), and that bottoms out in `Verse/RegionGrid.GetValidRegionAt`, whose FIRST\nline is\n\n    map.regionAndRoomUpdater.TryRebuildDirtyRegionsAndRooms();\n\nSo a read taken while the region grid is dirty does not observe — it FLUSHES a\npending rebuild. Two consequences, and the second is the one that matters:\n\n1. **`Room` objects are destroyed and recreated**, so the `room_id` an observer\n   published one call earlier can name a room that no longer exists. `room \u003cid\u003e`\n   already handles a missing id (`WorldSafe.FindRoom` refuses), but nothing says\n   the id is only valid until the next wall goes up.\n2. **`Verse/RegionAndRoomUpdater` -\u003e `Room.Notify_RoomShapeChanged` reaches\n   scribed state.** `Map.autoBuildRoofAreaSetter.TryGenerateAreaFor(room)` writes\n   the roof Area, and the bed pass sets `Building_Bed.ForPrisoners = true`. Both\n   are scribed. That is an OBSERVER WRITE by the project's own definition, and it\n   is not in the catalogue.\n\nIt also `Log.Warning`s when the updater is disabled and dirty, which would land\nin the journal as a red/yellow the run did not cause.\n\n## Where it is reachable from\n\n    grep -rn \"GetRoom(\" Source/AutoRimmer/\n\nat least: `DigestVerb.ColonistSection` (`pawn.GetRoom()`, per colonist, per\ndigest), `SpatialVerbs.RoomAt`, `PlaceVerbs` (`rooms`/`room`),\n`TemperatureVerbs.FillServed` and `FoodRot` (via `Thing.AmbientTemperature`).\n`digest` is evaluated on a per-frame predicate cadence inside `advance`, so this\nis a per-frame path.\n\n## Why it has never bitten\n\n`RegionAndRoomUpdater.TryRebuildDirtyRegionsAndRooms` is called by the game\nitself every `MapPreTick`, so the grid is clean for almost every read. The window\nis a read taken in the SAME FRAME as a wall being built, destroyed, or a door\nbeing installed — which is exactly what `place-layout` and `build` do, and\nexactly when an agent then reads the digest to see whether it worked.\n\n## The honest disposition\n\nThis is probably ACCEPTABLE and should be DOCUMENTED rather than fixed: the same\nruling `WorldSafe` already gives `Reachability.CanReach`'s cache fill,\n`CostListCalculator.cachedCosts` and `DangerWatcher.dangerRatingInt` — idempotent,\nRNG-free, and performed by the game itself constantly. But it is not currently\nwritten down anywhere, `WorldSafe.cs`'s hazard classes do not list it, and\n`Map.autoBuildRoofAreaSetter` writing a scribed Area is materially different from\nfilling a cache: it changes what a SAVE contains.\n\nThe decision to make is whether an observer is allowed to flush the region\nupdater at all, or whether the read path should ask\n`map.regionAndRoomUpdater.Enabled` / the dirty flag first and degrade to a null\nroom with a stated reason.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `WorldSafe.cs`'s hazard catalogue names this route explicitly, by member\n  (`RegionAndRoomQuery.GetRoom` -\u003e `RegionGrid.GetValidRegionAt` -\u003e\n  `RegionAndRoomUpdater.TryRebuildDirtyRegionsAndRooms`), and states which of the\n  two consequences above the project accepts and why.\n- DESIGN's decisions log carries the ruling, in the same shape as the existing\n  observer-write rulings, and says whether `autoBuildRoofAreaSetter`'s scribed\n  write changes the answer.\n- Either (a) the ruling is \"accepted, and here is why a save cannot differ\", with\n  the argument written out, or (b) the read path is changed and every caller\n  above is updated together — never one file at a time, because a partial fix\n  leaves the hazard with a comment saying it was handled.\n- `room_id`'s lifetime is stated wherever a room id is published (`rooms`,\n  `room`, `room-at`, `digest.temperature.rooms[*].room_id`): it is valid until\n  the region grid is rebuilt, which any construction can trigger.","files":null}]}